Neui is an AI agent and a web framework built as one stack. The core is a server-driven Go web framework (<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;doors-dev&#x2F;doors" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;doors-dev&#x2F;doors</a>); neui (<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;doors-dev&#x2F;neui" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;doors-dev&#x2F;neui</a>) turns each page into an agent harness.<p>FEATURES:<p><i>The agent sees &amp; operates UI.</i>
Annotate what agent can access (links, inputs, buttons), so agent sees it and can assist user with UI operations or even automate it with scripting.<p><pre><code>   ~&gt;neui.Use{ Desc:&quot;submit the form&quot; } &lt;button&gt;Submit&lt;&#x2F;button&gt;
</code></pre>
or expose context data for the agent:<p><pre><code>   &lt;div class=&quot;card&quot;&gt;
       ~neui.Data{Text: &quot;the product shown in the card&quot;, Object: product}
       ...
   &lt;&#x2F;div&gt;

</code></pre>
